A REQUEST (NOT A CONDITION)

The MIT-0 license above deliberately drops the attribution requirement: you are free
to use, modify and redistribute this mod, or code taken from it, **without crediting
anyone**. Nothing on this page adds any obligation beyond the license text.

That said — if KernelExtensions or code taken from it ends up in something you
publish, a mention would be genuinely appreciated. Something like:

    Uses code from KernelExtensions by LDTchara
    https://github.com/LDTchara/KernelExtensions

This is a courtesy, not a term of the license. You are not in breach of anything if
you skip it, and you do not need to ask permission either way.

WHY THIS FILE STILL NAMES A COPYRIGHT HOLDER

MIT-0 removes the *duty* to preserve the notice; it does not remove authorship. The
line at the top records who wrote this so the origin stays a matter of public record.
Claiming authorship of this work is a false statement rather than a licensing
question — and that was equally true under the MIT license this project used before.
